== Version 0.9.0 ==
[] Added Kalonymos, Shealtiel, Benveniste, Makhirite dynaties to the history files.
[] Split Beit Bostanai and Beit Anan to their own dynasty (Bostanites) From Davidite
[] Split Pinchas Ben Abdimi's line to its own dynasty (Beit Nathan)
[] Added playable landless administrative titles to all playable jewish dynasties
[] Gave playable landless jewish dynasties their own government type
[] Made the Exilarchates a figurehead title with its own succession election type
[] Added a decision to start a scheme to get a claim on the exilarchate title, so you may be elected it.
[] Fixed many title flavorizations issues
[] Expanded history for Maimonides, Made him playable
[] Fixed many bugs
[] Added new fancier CoA for the empire of Canaan

== Version 0.10.0 ==
[] Added Kingdom of Edom, with a decision to create it
[] Added Edomite culture
[] Reworked Dejure lines of Empire of Canaan
[] Allowed formation of Beth Nahrain for Israelites and Canaanites
[] Fixed a bug here tripoli was not selectable as a dejure capital for e_canaan
[] Restored missing Punic Holy Site
[] Added a decision to restore Edomite culture

== Version 0.10.1 ==
[] Added Compatibility with Cultures Expanded Mod

== Version 0.10.2 == 
[] Fixed A Bug with aramean culture history

== Version 0.11.0
[] Added the Empire of Kemet, consisting of Egypt, Nubia and Blemmyia, as well as a decision to create it.
[] Fixed a bug with Canaan Creation decision, where the capital selection event had localization issues, and did not move the defacto realm capital
[] Added effects of various decisions in this mode to be previewed when viewing the decisions.
[] Changed some traditions of Aramean and Phoenician cultures.
[] Added Copt Culture

== Version 0.12.0
[] Added Hegemony of the Fertile Crescent, and a decision to form it
[] Improved Events performance
[] Reworked Kemet Geographical Region Requirements
[] Added Lower and Upper Egypt Kingdoms
[] Changed some decision images
[] Fixed some Localizations

== Version 0.13.0
[] Added Masada special building (3 tiers) at the capital of Negev: Ruins → Restored Fortifications → Grand Masada
[] Added nicknames for Kemet and Fertile Crescent founders: "the Lord of Kemet" and "Lord of the Crescent"
[] Improved nickname descriptions for the Rising Lion/Lioness and Beth Nahrain
[] Expanded Mishpacha government description with historical Nasi and Exilarchate context
[] Jewish-flavored Exilarchate election vote tooltips (Nasi, Melech, Nagid) replacing generic feudal terms
[] Added a new icon for Mishpacha Government, instead of administrative one.
[] Moving the domicile of Mishpacha government now uses the travel system.

== Version 0.14.0 ==
[] Updated for Crusader Kings III 1.20 (faiths, rites and tenets moved to the new religion structure)
[] Copts now speak the vanilla Egyptian language instead of a separate Coptic one
[] Clearing the Temple grounds now removes Jerusalem as a holy site of the Islamic faiths
[] Mishpacha: rebalanced the government. Mercenaries are 25% cheaper instead of more expensive, and families gain +15% income, +10% influence and +10% learning lifestyle experience
[] Mishpacha: families are now vassals of the realm their estate lies in, under a new "Charter of Privileges" contract (communal taxes, religious rights, Beit Din rights, trade rights)
[] Mishpacha: families under a Muslim liege who taxes nonbelievers start paying jizya
[] Mishpacha: removed the title revocation protection option from the charter
[] Mishpacha: moving the estate to another realm makes the family a vassal of that realm's ruler
[] Mishpacha: the estate can be moved from the province view
[] Mishpacha: moving the estate takes longer (the whole family travels), and camp provision and herd travel events no longer fire for it
[] Mishpacha: a family that gains land adopts its liege's government, or feudal if there is none
[] Mishpacha: a family head who leaves Judaism steps down in favor of the nearest Jewish man of their house
[] Mishpacha: AI families now move to more welcoming realms on their own, when the new home is clearly better than staying
[] Mishpacha: added Mishpacha Succession, fixing family heads and Exilarchs who had no working succession
[] Added the "Expel the Jews" decision for Christian and Muslim rulers. Jewish families leave the realm, Jewish courtiers are dismissed, Jewish lords lose their lands, and half of every departing Jew's gold is seized
[] Expelled Jews may resist in a single shared war; a lord who surrenders becomes a landless Mishpacha family
[] Added the "Readmit the Jews" decision; edicts concerning the Jews have a 10-year cooldown
[] The AI decides on expulsion and readmission based on traits, rite tenets and personal tenets
[] Added notifications and a summary event for the ruler who expels the Jews
[] Added the Court Financier court position for non-Jewish dukes and above: raises domain taxes and Jewish opinion, angers zealots, and brings debt-collection events
[] Kohenism: replaced Communal Identity with the new Kehunah tenet (hereditary priesthood, tithes), with its own icon
[] Kohenism: the faith and its rite now agree on doctrines (the Kohen Gadol is a spiritual head)
[] Kohenism: new faith icon in the 1.20 style
[] Kohenism: High Priests keep the Kohen Gadol garments in their portraits after death, both historic ones and those who die in office during play
[] Fixed the Fertile Crescent region counting Levantine provinces twice
[] Fixed the Persian Struggle not including the Bavlim culture
[] Fixed many errors: Tanas holy site, Canaanite faith tenets, Lower Egypt adjective, Third Temple tenet check, Masada defense bonus, Maimonides' traits, Claim Exilarchate description, Semitic pagan religious head, and duplicate localization keys
